  "Earth": "NASA Earth Fact Sheet; temperatures: WMO records; dose rates: UNSCEAR 2008 (outdoor, sea level; equivalent dose without radon, ~0.27 uSv/h with it); composition: dry air; perigee / apogee = perihelion / aphelion",
  "Moon": "NASA Moon Fact Sheet; dose rates: Chang'e 4 Lunar Lander Neutrons and Dosimetry, Zhang et al., Science Advances 2020 (absorbed in silicon; 1369 uSv/day); pressure and composition: LADEE, exosphere (collisionless: no volume ratio); axial tilt 1.54 deg to the ecliptic; temperatures: Diviner (polar craters down to ~-248 C)",
  "Sun": "NASA Sun Fact Sheet; IAU 2015 nominal radius; rotation 25.38 d sidereal (Carrington), ~25 d at the equator to ~34 d at the poles; composition by number of atoms (photosphere); orbit around the galactic centre (~26000 ly, galactic year)"
